  "text": "Here's a complete implementation of the `remove_adjacent_duplicates` function, along with the test cases using `unittest`. This function iterates through the list and builds a new list by including only elements that are not the same as the previous one \u2014 that is, it removes consecutive duplicates.\n\n```python\nimport unittest\n\ndef remove_adjacent_duplicates(lst):\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n    result = [lst[0]]\n    for num in lst[1:]:\n        if num != result[-1]:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n\nclass TestRemoveAdjacentDuplicates(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_basic_functionality(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4]), [1, 2, 3, 4])\n    \n    def test_repeated_elements(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([5, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7]), [5, 6, 7])\n    \n    def test_multiple_duplicates(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5]), [1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- The function starts by checking if the input list is empty.\n- It initializes a result list with the first element of the input list.\n- Then it iterates through the rest of the elements and appends them to the result list only if they are different from the last item in the result list.\n- This ensures that consecutive duplicates are removed.\n\n### Output when run:\nThis script will run the tests and print the results to the console. If all tests pass, it will show:\n```\n.....\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 3 tests in 0.001s\n\nOK\n```\n\nLet me know if you'd like to extend the function to remove non-consecutive duplicates or have other variations!",
